// Pop signing configuration.
//
// THE ONE FILE that decides the app's code identity. It exists so that
// switching identity is a one-line edit rather than a hunt through project
// settings: Xcode → Settings → Accounts → Manage Certificates is where
// certificates live, and this file is where Pop picks one.

// The identity Pop signs with today. `PopDev` is a stable self-signed
// codesigning certificate in the login keychain (created 2026-10: 10-year,
// Code Signing EKU) — stable on purpose: Keychain ACLs bind to the code
// signature, and an identity that never changes means the user grants
// keychain access exactly once, not once per rebuild. `POP_SIGN_IDENTITY`
// env still overrides, e.g. `POP_SIGN_IDENTITY=GlanceDev ./Scripts/bundle_app.sh`.
//
// TO SHIP: once a "Developer ID Application" certificate exists in
// Xcode → Settings → Accounts → Manage Certificates, changing ONLY the next
// line to `Developer ID Application` is the entire edit required for a
// distributable, notarizable build.
POP_SIGN_IDENTITY = PopDev

// Xcode refuses to combine automatic signing with a named identity
// ("Pop is automatically signed, but code signing identity GlanceDev has been
// manually specified"), and automatic signing on a free Personal Team cannot
// produce a stable, portable identity anyway — the identity changes with the
// signed-in account, which is exactly the Keychain/TCC drift this file exists
// to stop.
//
// Manual signing is therefore the combination that both BUILDS and gives a
// stable code identity, and it still leaves the identity under Xcode's control:
// it is chosen in Signing & Capabilities and set in ONE line below.
CODE_SIGN_STYLE = Manual
CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY = $(POP_SIGN_IDENTITY)

// Intentionally EMPTY. Manual signing with a named identity needs no team, and
// naming one would make Xcode reject a self-signed certificate ("No certificate
// for team '...' matching 'GlanceDev' found"). Xcode fills the team itself once
// POP_SIGN_IDENTITY above is a real team certificate such as
// "Developer ID Application".
DEVELOPMENT_TEAM =

// Pop is an accessory app that drives other applications and reads system
// state, so the hardened runtime is required for a notarized build. It is not
// sandboxed and must not be.
ENABLE_HARDENED_RUNTIME = YES
CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS = Config/Pop.entitlements